\subsection{Refined first law: cycle enhancement}
\label{sec:cycle_enhancement}

The high-resolution tree-graph scans transform the first law of Silent Discordance from a binary ``cycle necessity'' to a quantitative ``cycle enhancement'':

\textbf{First law (refined): law of cycle enhancement.} Silent Discordance is present in both cyclic and acyclic structures, but its stability, depth, and robustness against scan resolution are enhanced by the presence of cycles. In acyclic structures, the valley exists but is narrower and more sensitive to grid resolution; its position is determined by the geometric properties of the tree (branching number, radius) rather than by a simple ``cycle/no-cycle'' dichotomy.

This refinement is not a weakening of the original law. It is a sharpening: the original ``cycle necessity'' was an artifact of low scan resolution, and the corrected law provides a quantitative measure (valley width, depth, robustness) that distinguishes cyclic from acyclic structures while acknowledging that both support the phenomenon.

\textbf{Honest limitation:} The high-resolution tree-graph scans were performed only at $N=7$ with exact diagonalization. Whether the valley persists at larger tree sizes, and whether its position scales with tree geometry in a universal way, remains open. The falsification test used only one random seed for non-star topologies in the depth analysis; the seed dependence is reported but not yet statistically characterized.

\section{Non-Equilibrium Survival}
\label{sec:non_eq}

\subsection{Experimental design}
\label{sec:non_eq_design}

To test whether Silent Discordance survives away from thermal equilibrium, we constructed a non-equilibrium steady state by applying opposite magnetic fields ($+\mu$ on the left half, $-\mu$ on the right half) to a chain of $L=20$ sites with a central contradiction edge. The scan is performed as in the equilibrium case.

The predefined success criterion is: if the enhanced diagnosis shows a non-monotonic extremum while the default diagnosis remains smooth, Silent Discordance survives in the non-equilibrium steady state.

